  "response_text": "To allocate the stack value we need to first determine how big to make the stack. Once this is chosen we can simply subtract that size from the MSP_init_val and then we have the PSP_val. We need to know the location of MSP first so that we can put the PSP_val inside of memory without overwriting any start up code and so that it is on a valid location, one where the memory is a multiple of 8, which can be done as MSP_init_val is known. We also need to know the MSP_init_val because if we just choose a random place we don\u2019t know how big the stack is.\\n",
